WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:04.870 line:0%
<i> If hell is the lowest and
 hottest place in America,</i>

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.940 line:0%
<i> and heaven the highest,</i>

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.710 line:0%
<i> then everything in between
 is purgatory.</i>

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:16.048 line:0%
<i> Now, dance with the devil.</i>

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.518 line:0%
<i> From Death Valley...</i>

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.619 line:0%
<i> to Mount Whitney.</i>

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:24.657 line:0%
<i> 146 miles of gross scraps...</i>

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.293 line:0%
<i> painful naps...</i>

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.429 line:0%
<i> and deadly traps.</i>

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.700 line:0%
<i> This is a tale of survival...</i>

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:40.373 line:0%
<i> ...between two great extremes.</i>

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:45.511 line:0%
(music:<i> America the Beautiful)</i>

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.546
(music)

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.884
(music)

00:00:55.221 --> 00:01:01.327 line:0%
(music)

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:05.298 line:0%
<i> Here lies a valley
 called death.</i>

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:10.870 line:0%
<i> It's the hottest place
 in America.</i>

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:18.678 line:0%
<i> A fine summer's day can hit
 130 degrees-plus.</i>

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.751 line:0%
<i> It has all the desert and
 desperation you'd expect.</i>

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:31.691 line:0%
<i> Plants have a tenuous
 grip on life.</i>

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:37.163 line:0%
<i> Animals appear
 just as stressed.</i>

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.198 line:0%
(music)

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:44.336 line:0%
(music)

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:48.274 line:0%
<i> So, when the going gets tough,</i>

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:53.012 line:0%
<i> the tough do a round
 at the golf course.</i>

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.549 line:0%
(music)

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.618 line:0%
<i> It's not a mirage,</i>

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:02.888 line:0%
<i> but a surreal man-made oasis,</i>

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:08.027 line:0%
<i> nurtured by thousands of
 gallons of underground water.</i>

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.429 line:0%
<i> There are hazards here.</i>

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.266 line:0%
<i> Especially for the wildlife.</i>

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:17.303 line:0%
<i> Only a privileged few coyotes
 are brave enough</i>

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.440 line:0%
<i> to take a swing
 at this high life.</i>

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:28.014 line:0%
<i> But their rewards are
 liquid refreshments.</i>

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:31.151 line:0%
<i> And maybe a birdie.</i>

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:40.092 line:0%
(music)

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:46.132 line:0%
(music)

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:53.139 line:0%
(music)

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:57.143 line:0%
<i> Problem is, roadrunners
 don't just run.</i>

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.318 line:0%
(music)

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:13.192 line:0%
(music)

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:17.197 line:0%
<i> Another young coyote takes
 a shot close to a water hazard.</i>

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.734 line:0%
<i> A flock of ibis.</i>

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:26.839 line:0%
(music)

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:31.210 line:0%
<i> This lake may be the most
 lethal trap on the course.</i>

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.846 line:0%
(music)

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:39.885 line:0%
(music)

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:44.490 line:0%
(music)

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:49.795 line:0%
<i> His scorecard's not
 looking too good.</i>

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:52.865 line:0%
<i> He may need some more
 lessons from mom.</i>

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:59.138 line:0%
<i> A coyote pup that
 can't fend for itself</i>

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.774 line:0%
<i> wants whatever mom brings home.</i>

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:08.647 line:0%
<i> If that's not enough,
 forget golf.</i>

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:10.716 line:0%
(music)

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:16.755 line:0%
(music)

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:23.362 line:0%
(music)

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:28.400 line:0%
<i> The pup that scored the old
 deer skull draws attention.</i>

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.103 line:0%
(music)

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:37.710 line:0%
(music)

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:42.348 line:0%
<i> Real flesh and bone is a prized
 possession in coyote land.</i>

00:04:45.984 --> 00:04:48.487 line:0%
<i> To keep something
 like a rabbit skin,</i>

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:51.891 line:0%
<i> you gotta turn it
 into buried treasure.</i>

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:57.563 line:0%
(music)

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:04.303 line:0%
(music)

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:07.072 line:0%
<i> But a pirate watches.</i>

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:10.376 line:0%
(music)

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:16.949 line:0%
(music)

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:20.920 line:0%
<i> There's nothing worse than
 taking your eye off the ball.</i>

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:27.693 line:0%
(music)

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:30.729 line:0%
(music)

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:36.735 line:0%
(music)

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:43.242 line:0%
(music)

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:48.881 line:0%
<i> The 19th hole is what
 golfers call the bar.</i>

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:53.453 line:0%
<i> And there's one out here
 offering a top-shelf cocktail.</i>

00:05:55.254 --> 00:06:00.460 line:0%
<i> A single date palm tree can
 produce 300 pounds of dates.</i>

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:06.599 line:0%
<i> The ripest treats
 litter the ground.</i>

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:10.736 line:0%
<i> Their sweet smell
 is a siren song.</i>

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:14.240 line:0%
<i> And fruit flies answer.</i>

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.476 line:0%
<i> But there's a problem.</i>

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:22.281 line:0%
<i> After a long journey
 through the desert,</i>

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.851 line:0%
<i> they risk overdoing it.</i>

00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:32.925 line:0%
<i> Each date is almost 80% sugar.</i>

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:39.331 line:0%
<i> Which ferments in the sun.</i>

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:42.635 line:0%
<i> The results are intoxicating.</i>

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.975 line:0%
<i> The fun fruit fly party
 gets out of hand.</i>

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:56.716 line:0%
<i> And this is a bad place
 for a bender.</i>

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:03.522 line:0%
<i> Below is a sobering sand trap.</i>

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:08.593 line:0%
(music)

00:07:08.593 --> 00:07:12.064 line:0%
<i> It reminds everyone
 that Death Valley</i>

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.700 line:0%
<i> includes the D word.</i>

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:22.975 line:0%
<i> This alien-looking insect larva
 is called an antlion.</i>

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:27.780 line:0%
<i> It digs its home
 with steep walls.</i>

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.985 line:0%
<i> All he needs is a tipsy
 fruit fly to stagger close by.</i>

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.020 line:0%
(music)

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:41.393 line:0%
(music)

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:45.330 line:0%
<i> One wrong step, and...</i>

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:51.003 line:0%
(music)

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:53.872 line:0%
<i> There's no escape.</i>

00:07:53.872 --> 00:07:57.743 line:0%
<i> The antlion's jaws
 grip like a vise.</i>

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:04.617 line:0%
<i> And more, they are hollow,
 like syringes.</i>

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:11.424 line:0%
<i> It injects powerful enzymes
 deep inside its prey.</i>

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:18.630 line:0%
<i> They liquefy the fly's insides.</i>

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:23.302 line:0%
(music)

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:29.108 line:0%
<i> After the enzymes are done,
 the antlion reverses the flow,</i>

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:32.912 line:0%
<i> sucking out every
 last bit of goo.</i>

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:41.120 line:0%
<i> Soon, the fly is nothing more
 than an empty shell.</i>

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.155 line:0%
(music)

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:48.527 line:0%
(music)

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:52.698 line:0%
<i> After ditching the evidence,</i>

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:56.368 line:0%
<i> it readies itself for
 the next drunken victim.</i>

00:08:56.368 --> 00:09:03.175 line:0%
(music)

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:05.845 line:0%
<i> The antlion will continue
 to trap its food</i>

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:09.414 line:0%
<i> for years to come.</i>

00:09:09.414 --> 00:09:11.516 line:0%
<i> Eventually, it'll transform</i>

00:09:11.516 --> 00:09:14.887 line:0%
<i> into a large, harmless
 fly itself.</i>

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:20.459 line:0%
<i> And buzz off to discover
 the harsh realities</i>

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:23.863 line:0%
<i> of life beyond this oasis.</i>

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:31.870 line:0%
<i> Death Valley is the lowest
 point in North America,</i>

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.107 line:0%
<i> and the hottest.</i>

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:40.178 line:0%
<i> The golf course sits in the
 middle of this sunbaked park.</i>

00:09:40.178 --> 00:09:44.449 line:0%
<i> Yet travel just 105 miles west</i>

00:09:44.449 --> 00:09:47.653 line:0%
<i> and you reach Mount Whitney,</i>

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:51.190 line:0%
<i> the highest point
 in the Lower 48,</i>

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.592 line:0%
<i> and still rising.</i>

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:58.664 line:0%
<i> The path between these points
 is a journey of great extremes.</i>

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:05.071 line:0%
<i> Some folks can't wait
 to check it out.</i>

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:14.079 line:0%
<i> Once a year, madmen and women
 line up in Death Valley</i>

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:16.782 line:0%
<i> to do the unthinkable.</i>

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:21.587 line:0%
<i> 100 athletes from 20 states
 and 19 different countries</i>

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:26.125 line:0%
<i> compete in perhaps the world's
 most grueling foot race.</i>

00:10:26.125 --> 00:10:32.131 line:0%
(cheering)

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:37.569 line:0%
<i> The Badwater Ultramarathon
 is 135 miles long.</i>

00:10:37.569 --> 00:10:43.775 line:0%
(music)

00:10:43.775 --> 00:10:50.249 line:0%
<i> It starts at Badwater Basin,
 280 feet below sea level.</i>

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:54.253 line:0%
<i> Only one way to go from here...</i>

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:56.022 line:0%
<i> up.</i>

00:10:57.889 --> 00:11:00.760 line:0%
<i> The humans are doing it tough.</i>

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:06.999 line:0%
<i> Not everyone out here
 is in such a hurry.</i>

00:11:09.735 --> 00:11:13.639 line:0%
<i> You might say this is
 no country for old men.</i>

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:21.547 line:0%
<i> But for one old-timer out here,
 it's a different story.</i>

00:11:25.751 --> 00:11:29.588 line:0%
(music)

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:34.360 line:0%
<i> After more than 40 years in
 California's Death Valley...</i>

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:39.698 line:0%
<i> this old tortoise has
 learned a trick or two</i>

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.468 line:0%
<i> about survival in the desert.</i>

00:11:45.136 --> 00:11:48.707 line:0%
<i> Like seize the shade
 while you have it.</i>

00:11:48.707 --> 00:11:54.646 line:0%
(music)

00:11:54.646 --> 00:11:59.185 line:0%
<i> He's just a bit bigger
 than a football.</i>

00:11:59.185 --> 00:12:02.487 line:0%
<i> And he grows less than
 an eighth of an inch each year.</i>

00:12:02.487 --> 00:12:07.892 line:0%
(music)

00:12:07.892 --> 00:12:11.830 line:0%
<i> He forages when it's cooler,</i>

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:16.268 line:0%
<i> especially in spring and fall,</i>

00:12:16.268 --> 00:12:20.806 line:0%
<i> and feasts on grass,
 flowers and shrubs.</i>

00:12:20.806 --> 00:12:23.808 line:0%
(music)

00:12:23.808 --> 00:12:26.511 line:0%
<i> Even some cactus now and then.</i>

00:12:26.511 --> 00:12:28.547 line:0%
(music)

00:12:28.547 --> 00:12:33.685 line:0%
(music)

00:12:33.685 --> 00:12:38.157 line:0%
<i> If he's lucky, there's some
 moisture in the plants he eats,</i>

00:12:38.157 --> 00:12:41.693 line:0%
<i> but he can also go a full year
 without a drink.</i>

00:12:41.693 --> 00:12:45.163 line:0%
(music)

00:12:45.163 --> 00:12:51.169 line:0%
(music)

00:12:51.169 --> 00:12:54.906 line:0%
<i> He's not in any speed race.</i>

00:12:54.906 --> 00:12:58.410 line:0%
<i> Flat out, it takes him
 around five hours</i>

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:01.280 line:0%
<i> to cover a single mile.</i>

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:07.887 line:0%
<i> But he is built
 for off-road endurance.</i>

00:13:09.722 --> 00:13:12.724 line:0%
<i> Those limbs may look
 a bit clunky,</i>

00:13:12.724 --> 00:13:16.461 line:0%
<i> but they are powerful tools,</i>

00:13:16.461 --> 00:13:20.399 line:0%
<i> with strong claws for
 his most important duty.</i>

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:33.711 line:0%
<i> He digs burrows
 to escape the heat.</i>

00:13:33.711 --> 00:13:38.383 line:0%
<i> Some go as deep as six feet.</i>

00:13:38.383 --> 00:13:43.622 line:0%
<i> This trip topside is
 more of an anomaly.</i>

00:13:43.622 --> 00:13:45.424 line:0%
<i> Desert tortoises spend</i>

00:13:45.424 --> 00:13:50.429 line:0%
<i> an incredible 95% of
 their lives underground.</i>

00:13:53.132 --> 00:13:57.403 line:0%
<i> Come winter, he may share a den
 with several others.</i>

00:13:59.271 --> 00:14:02.675 line:0%
<i> And maybe find a mate
 for the spring.</i>

00:14:14.119 --> 00:14:18.057 line:0%
<i> Nothing escapes the sun
 in Death Valley.</i>

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:23.928 line:0%
<i> It defines life
 from the rocky outcrops</i>

00:14:23.928 --> 00:14:27.266 line:0%
<i> to the fine sand of the dunes.</i>

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.837 line:0%
<i> When the sun peaks in the sky,</i>

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:36.608 line:0%
<i> the ground can exceed
 200 degrees Fahrenheit,</i>

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:40.346 line:0%
<i> almost hot enough
 to boil blood.</i>

00:14:43.548 --> 00:14:45.550 line:0%
<i> That's why those
 marathon runners</i>

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.620 line:0%
<i> began in the cool
 of the evening,</i>

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:51.957 line:0%
<i> and now run into the dark.</i>

00:14:53.925 --> 00:14:57.429 line:0%
<i> It's the best way
 to beat the heat.</i>

00:14:57.429 --> 00:15:00.398 line:0%
<i> In winter, Death Valley
 night temperatures</i>

00:15:00.398 --> 00:15:03.269 line:0%
<i> can drop to below freezing.</i>

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.572 line:0%
<i> But it's mid-July.</i>

00:15:07.572 --> 00:15:11.310 line:0%
<i> At 3:00 AM,
 it's still in the 70s.</i>

00:15:15.714 --> 00:15:19.618 line:0%
<i> Just off the road,
 other creatures of the night</i>

00:15:19.618 --> 00:15:23.288 line:0%
<i> also take advantage
 of the temperature dip.</i>

00:15:23.288 --> 00:15:28.460 line:0%
(music)

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:31.696 line:0%
<i> The desert kangaroo rat
 is built to survive</i>

00:15:31.696 --> 00:15:34.700 line:0%
<i> in this unforgiving world.</i>

00:15:36.702 --> 00:15:39.638 line:0%
<i> She has special kidneys
 that dispose of waste</i>

00:15:39.638 --> 00:15:43.441 line:0%
<i> without sacrificing much water.</i>

00:15:43.441 --> 00:15:49.481 line:0%
<i> And unlike all other mammals,
 she doesn't sweat to keep cool.</i>

00:15:51.016 --> 00:15:54.086 line:0%
<i> Her ears, although small,</i>

00:15:54.086 --> 00:15:58.791 line:0%
<i> can detect almost
 any approaching predator.</i>

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:03.595 line:0%
<i> Helpful when danger glides
 across the dunes.</i>

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:08.300 line:0%
(rattling)

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.869 line:0%
<i> They call him sidewinder,</i>

00:16:10.869 --> 00:16:14.440 line:0%
<i> one of the desert's
 deadliest gunslingers.</i>

00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:22.581 line:0%
<i> He packs two fangs capable
 of delivering a venomous bite.</i>

00:16:22.581 --> 00:16:26.351 line:0%
(music)

00:16:26.351 --> 00:16:29.321 line:0%
<i> The sand is still
 painfully hot,</i>

00:16:29.321 --> 00:16:32.324 line:0%
<i> but this rattler has adapted.</i>

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:35.927 line:0%
<i> By moving side to side
 instead of slithering,</i>

00:16:35.927 --> 00:16:37.862 line:0%
<i> he only ever makes contact</i>

00:16:37.862 --> 00:16:41.633 line:0%
<i> with two points of his body
 at a time.</i>

00:16:41.633 --> 00:16:45.804 line:0%
(music)

00:16:45.804 --> 00:16:49.742 line:0%
<i> The kangaroo rat also
 gets a lot of airtime.</i>

00:16:52.343 --> 00:16:56.247 line:0%
<i> She can jump up to nine feet
 in one hop</i>

00:16:56.247 --> 00:17:00.619 line:0%
<i> as she bounces through the
 brush on her hunt for seeds.</i>

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:03.121 line:0%
(rattling)

00:17:03.121 --> 00:17:05.157 line:0%
<i> When these two face off...</i>

00:17:05.157 --> 00:17:09.227 line:0%
(rattling)

00:17:09.227 --> 00:17:14.032 line:0%
<i> It all comes down
 to the quickest draw.</i>

00:17:14.032 --> 00:17:15.634 line:0%
(rattling)

00:17:20.472 --> 00:17:23.909 line:0%
(rattling)

00:17:23.909 --> 00:17:27.813 line:0%
<i> The sidewinder is one of
 the most dangerous creatures</i>

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:31.350 line:0%
<i> in California's Death Valley.</i>

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.052 line:0%
<i> The kangaroo rat,</i>

00:17:34.052 --> 00:17:36.922 line:0%
<i> within striking distance,</i>

00:17:36.922 --> 00:17:38.957 line:0%
<i> is in big trouble.</i>

00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:44.529 line:0%
(music)

00:17:44.529 --> 00:17:47.999 line:0%
<i> Close, but no strike.</i>

00:17:47.999 --> 00:17:52.637 line:0%
<i> The kangaroo rat manages
 to dodge death.</i>

00:17:52.637 --> 00:17:55.107 line:0%
<i> Almost all of these encounters</i>

00:17:55.107 --> 00:17:58.710 line:0%
<i> favor her lightning-fast
 reflexes.</i>

00:18:02.113 --> 00:18:06.518 line:0%
<i> The sidewinder looks
 for another meal.</i>

00:18:06.518 --> 00:18:08.620 line:0%
<i> And sure enough,</i>

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:13.192 line:0%
<i> at dawn he finds a second duel.</i>

00:18:16.361 --> 00:18:20.065 line:0%
<i> But this roadrunner
 is no chicken.</i>

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:26.338 line:0%
<i> Around here, she's the law.</i>

00:18:26.338 --> 00:18:28.373 line:0%
(music)

00:18:28.373 --> 00:18:33.645 line:0%
(music)

00:18:33.645 --> 00:18:38.249 line:0%
<i> It's fang versus beak.</i>

00:18:38.249 --> 00:18:43.755 line:0%
(music)

00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:48.860 line:0%
<i> The sidewinder may have
 deadly venom,</i>

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:52.164 line:0%
<i> but the roadrunner is fearless.</i>

00:18:52.164 --> 00:18:57.068 line:0%
(rattling)

00:18:57.068 --> 00:18:59.104 line:0%
(music)

00:18:59.104 --> 00:19:04.476 line:0%
(music)

00:19:04.476 --> 00:19:09.514 line:0%
<i> This hero of the West
 barely blinks an eye.</i>

00:19:09.514 --> 00:19:11.950 line:0%
(music)

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:17.489 line:0%
(music)

00:19:17.489 --> 00:19:20.292 line:0%
<i> And she keeps on running.</i>

00:19:22.627 --> 00:19:27.032 line:0%
<i> The sun rises after 5:00 AM</i>

00:19:27.032 --> 00:19:29.501 line:0%
<i> and so does the mercury.</i>

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:36.041 line:0%
<i> Soon it's 98 degrees.</i>

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:40.412 line:0%
<i> As the ultramarathon runners
 pass the 40-mile marker,</i>

00:19:40.412 --> 00:19:43.782 line:0%
<i> many slow to a walk.</i>

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:49.487 line:0%
<i> No athlete can run
 135 miles nonstop,</i>

00:19:49.487 --> 00:19:53.258 line:0%
<i> especially in the hottest place
 in America.</i>

00:19:55.527 --> 00:20:01.299 line:0%
<i> Runners can drink close to
 a gallon of fluid every hour.</i>

00:20:01.299 --> 00:20:05.537 line:0%
<i> They call out for hydration.</i>

00:20:05.537 --> 00:20:10.409 line:0%
<i> Behind them,
 the Mesquite Sand Dunes.</i>

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:16.214 line:0%
<i> Here, and throughout
 Death Valley,</i>

00:20:16.214 --> 00:20:22.220 line:0%
<i> iconic mountains of sculpted
 sand hide among the landscape.</i>

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:27.892 line:0%
(music)

00:20:27.892 --> 00:20:32.163 line:0%
<i> Some are more than
 600 feet high</i>

00:20:32.163 --> 00:20:34.866 line:0%
<i> and constantly reforming.</i>

00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:39.304 line:0%
(wind blowing)

00:20:39.304 --> 00:20:43.074 line:0%
<i> They move with the wind.</i>

00:20:43.074 --> 00:20:45.643 line:0%
<i> Plants on the edges
 don't survive long</i>

00:20:45.643 --> 00:20:48.513 line:0%
<i> once a dune moves their way.</i>

00:20:48.513 --> 00:20:53.885 line:0%
(wind whistling)

00:20:53.885 --> 00:20:56.855 line:0%
<i> They are a sight to behold.</i>

00:20:56.855 --> 00:21:02.426 line:0%
(music)

00:21:02.426 --> 00:21:06.965 line:0%
<i> And in one case, also a sound.</i>

00:21:08.833 --> 00:21:12.604 line:0%
<i> The Eureka Dunes near
 the north end of the park</i>

00:21:12.604 --> 00:21:16.574 line:0%
<i> sing aloud with
 a booming voice.</i>

00:21:16.574 --> 00:21:20.211 line:0%
<i> This is what they sound like.</i>

00:21:20.211 --> 00:21:25.250 line:0%
(low humming and whistling)

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:31.622 line:0%
(low humming and whistling)

00:21:31.622 --> 00:21:34.892 line:0%
<i> The sand grains of Eureka Dune
 are dryer</i>

00:21:34.892 --> 00:21:39.463 line:0%
<i> and more loosely packed
 than most.</i>

00:21:39.463 --> 00:21:43.468 line:0%
<i> And they're mixed
 with very little dust.</i>

00:21:43.468 --> 00:21:46.804 line:0%
<i> When they shift,
 the friction between them</i>

00:21:46.804 --> 00:21:49.474 line:0%
<i> creates an acoustic airwave...</i>

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:56.214 line:0%
(low humming)

00:21:56.214 --> 00:21:59.684 line:0%
<i> ...that sounds like
 a groan or a hum.</i>

00:21:59.684 --> 00:22:02.821 line:0%
<i> Sometimes a boom.</i>

00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:08.360 line:0%
<i> It's a Death Valley serenade.</i>

00:22:10.728 --> 00:22:13.898 line:0%
<i> Inside dunes like this,</i>

00:22:13.898 --> 00:22:16.935 line:0%
<i> one of the park's
 best-equipped creatures</i>

00:22:16.935 --> 00:22:19.805 line:0%
<i> prepares to meet the day.</i>

00:22:24.108 --> 00:22:30.047 line:0%
<i> He uses the rays of the sun
 to get his juices flowing.</i>

00:22:30.047 --> 00:22:32.684 line:0%
<i> And once the coast is clear...</i>

00:22:32.684 --> 00:22:34.118 line:0%
(music)

00:22:34.118 --> 00:22:40.158 line:0%
(music)

00:22:40.158 --> 00:22:47.031 line:0%
(music)

00:22:47.031 --> 00:22:51.369 line:0%
<i> This is the Mojave
 fringe-toed lizard,</i>

00:22:51.369 --> 00:22:55.874 line:0%
<i> a master of desert survival.</i>

00:22:55.874 --> 00:23:00.044 line:0%
<i> He's got the best camouflage
 in North America.</i>

00:23:00.044 --> 00:23:03.714 line:0%
<i> So, it's hard to distinguish
 this medium-sized lizard</i>

00:23:03.714 --> 00:23:07.285 line:0%
<i> from the sand surrounding him.</i>

00:23:07.285 --> 00:23:12.323 line:0%
<i> Flaps over his ears and nose
 along with overlapping eyelids</i>

00:23:12.323 --> 00:23:17.395 line:0%
<i> work like valves
 to block pesky sand.</i>

00:23:17.395 --> 00:23:22.300 line:0%
<i> But his best feature
 just might be his namesake.</i>

00:23:24.402 --> 00:23:27.706 line:0%
<i> Those fringed toes.</i>

00:23:27.706 --> 00:23:34.045 line:0%
<i> A special adaption that
 helps him stay above the sand.</i>

00:23:34.045 --> 00:23:37.215 line:0%
<i> Comb-like scales
 on the edge of his toes</i>

00:23:37.215 --> 00:23:41.386 line:0%
<i> turn this lizard's feet
 into snowshoes on sand.</i>

00:23:44.122 --> 00:23:47.259 line:0%
<i> So he runs without
 burning his feet.</i>

00:23:50.394 --> 00:23:53.331 line:0%
<i> He doesn't even sink
 below the surface,</i>

00:23:53.331 --> 00:23:59.003 line:0%
<i> thus giving the fringe-toed
 lizard one more advantage:</i>

00:23:59.003 --> 00:24:01.907 line:0%
<i> speed.</i>

00:24:01.907 --> 00:24:06.244 line:0%
<i> The fastest was clocked
 at 23 miles per hour.</i>

00:24:06.244 --> 00:24:11.750 line:0%
<i> At that speed, the lizard is
 almost completely on two feet.</i>

00:24:14.619 --> 00:24:17.355 line:0%
<i> Temps skyrocket.</i>

00:24:17.355 --> 00:24:22.861 line:0%
<i> The Mojave fringe-toed lizard
 must call it a day.</i>

00:24:22.861 --> 00:24:26.398 line:0%
<i> So, he heads to the coolest
 place he can find.</i>

00:24:28.533 --> 00:24:31.436 line:0%
<i> Where no one even
 knows he's there.</i>

00:24:31.436 --> 00:24:37.442 line:0%
(music)

00:24:37.442 --> 00:24:42.180 line:0%
<i> Few can handle the midday heat
 out in the open.</i>

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:45.483 line:0%
<i> But the fringed-toed lizard
 has a cousin</i>

00:24:45.483 --> 00:24:48.687 line:0%
<i> who is a most extraordinary
 exception.</i>

00:24:53.591 --> 00:24:57.862 line:0%
<i> In California's Death Valley,
 the desert horned lizard</i>

00:24:57.862 --> 00:25:02.400 line:0%
<i> must hunt when
 his prey is active.</i>

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:04.035 line:0%
<i> And he's picky.</i>

00:25:04.035 --> 00:25:09.507 line:0%
<i> He really only eats
 one thing: ants.</i>

00:25:09.507 --> 00:25:13.044 line:0%
<i> Ants for breakfast,
 ants for lunch,</i>

00:25:13.044 --> 00:25:17.014 line:0%
<i> and ants for dinner.</i>

00:25:17.014 --> 00:25:19.550 line:0%
<i> Harvester ants make up 90%</i>

00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:23.354 line:0%
<i> of the desert
 horned lizard's diet.</i>

00:25:23.354 --> 00:25:27.659 line:0%
<i> But these insects are
 pretty tough themselves.</i>

00:25:30.128 --> 00:25:32.230 line:0%
<i> And they have numbers
 on their side.</i>

00:25:32.230 --> 00:25:39.237 line:0%
(music)

00:25:39.237 --> 00:25:43.975 line:0%
<i> Each colony has around
 10,000 individuals,</i>

00:25:43.975 --> 00:25:48.980 line:0%
<i> and each individual packs
 a painful bee-like sting.</i>

00:25:51.483 --> 00:25:54.218 line:0%
<i> Some ants will scurry
 more than 40 yards</i>

00:25:54.218 --> 00:25:56.754 line:0%
<i> to collect seeds for the nest.</i>

00:25:56.754 --> 00:26:01.459 line:0%
(music)

00:26:01.459 --> 00:26:07.398 line:0%
<i> So the lizard has the best luck
 on the outskirts of the colony</i>

00:26:07.398 --> 00:26:10.101 line:0%
<i> and plucks off a passerby.</i>

00:26:10.101 --> 00:26:12.136 line:0%
(music)

00:26:12.136 --> 00:26:17.542 line:0%
(music)

00:26:17.542 --> 00:26:22.413 line:0%
<i> But he can't afford
 to fall asleep on the job.</i>

00:26:22.413 --> 00:26:26.585 line:0%
<i> A couple spot him
 and fearlessly move in.</i>

00:26:29.887 --> 00:26:35.226 line:0%
<i> His scales are
 as tough as nails;</i>

00:26:35.226 --> 00:26:37.195 line:0%
<i> fingernails that is.</i>

00:26:37.195 --> 00:26:41.032 line:0%
<i> Each one is like a mini shield.</i>

00:26:41.032 --> 00:26:45.704 line:0%
<i> But a harvester ant can
 get under anyone's skin.</i>

00:26:47.439 --> 00:26:49.874 line:0%
<i> And then...</i>

00:26:49.874 --> 00:26:52.109 line:0%
<i> bite in.</i>

00:26:52.109 --> 00:26:56.247 line:0%
<i> It's an alarm clock with
 a piercing wake-up call.</i>

00:26:56.247 --> 00:27:02.587 line:0%
(music)

00:27:02.587 --> 00:27:09.026 line:0%
<i> The human runners out here
 are also suffering.</i>

00:27:09.026 --> 00:27:12.096 line:0%
<i> Most of the Badwater
 Ultramarathon runners</i>

00:27:12.096 --> 00:27:14.566 line:0%
<i> are still going.</i>

00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:19.904 line:0%
<i> But at 70 miles in,</i>

00:27:19.904 --> 00:27:23.374 line:0%
<i> the long, hot road
 to the base of Mount Whitney</i>

00:27:23.374 --> 00:27:27.478 line:0%
<i> takes its toll.</i>

00:27:27.478 --> 00:27:32.117 line:0%
<i> By the end of the race, one
 quarter will have dropped out.</i>

00:27:34.752 --> 00:27:37.989 line:0%
<i> The option plays on the mind.</i>

00:27:42.993 --> 00:27:45.930 line:0%
<i> They have more than
 50 miles to go</i>

00:27:45.930 --> 00:27:48.299 line:0%
<i> when they exit
 the national park</i>

00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:53.404 line:0%
<i> with still plenty of desert
 to endure.</i>

00:27:53.404 --> 00:27:57.475 line:0%
<i> Not even realizing
 they're moving past a lake.</i>

00:28:03.415 --> 00:28:05.483 line:0%
<i> Owen's Lake.</i>

00:28:07.552 --> 00:28:11.489 line:0%
<i> At least this is what passes
 for a lake around here.</i>

00:28:14.859 --> 00:28:20.031 line:0%
<i> 120 years ago, water filled
 this salty basin.</i>

00:28:22.733 --> 00:28:26.471 line:0%
<i> And towns and mines
 surrounded it.</i>

00:28:28.206 --> 00:28:30.908 line:0%
<i> But engineers built an aqueduct</i>

00:28:30.908 --> 00:28:34.379 line:0%
<i> to divert the flow
 to Los Angeles.</i>

00:28:36.447 --> 00:28:38.850 line:0%
<i> And arsenic from
 the ancient lakebed</i>

00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:42.053 line:0%
<i> turned it into
 a toxic dust bowl.</i>

00:28:42.053 --> 00:28:44.088 line:0%
(music)

00:28:44.088 --> 00:28:49.360 line:0%
(music)

00:28:49.360 --> 00:28:51.395 line:0%
<i> Too dangerous to inhale.</i>

00:28:51.395 --> 00:28:55.032 line:0%
(music)

00:28:55.032 --> 00:28:57.668 line:0%
<i> Now, to solve that problem,</i>

00:28:57.668 --> 00:29:00.805 line:0%
<i> engineers have turned
 the tap back on.</i>

00:29:00.805 --> 00:29:07.645 line:0%
(music)

00:29:07.645 --> 00:29:11.916 line:0%
<i> And life is returning
 with the water,</i>

00:29:11.916 --> 00:29:14.619 line:0%
<i> starting with brine flies.</i>

00:29:14.619 --> 00:29:16.654 line:0%
(flies buzzing)

00:29:16.654 --> 00:29:23.561 line:0%
(flies buzzing)

00:29:23.561 --> 00:29:27.932 line:0%
<i> They hatch here in April
 and throughout the summer.</i>

00:29:27.932 --> 00:29:32.703 line:0%
(flies buzzing)

00:29:32.703 --> 00:29:37.908 line:0%
<i> And then birds
 come to eat them.</i>

00:29:37.908 --> 00:29:40.945 line:0%
(squawking)

00:29:40.945 --> 00:29:47.151 line:0%
(squawking)

00:29:47.151 --> 00:29:51.555 line:0%
(music)

00:29:51.555 --> 00:29:53.190 line:0%
<i> Gulls.</i>

00:29:53.190 --> 00:29:55.226 line:0%
(music)

00:29:55.226 --> 00:30:01.632 line:0%
(music)

00:30:01.632 --> 00:30:03.667 line:0%
<i> Ibis.</i>

00:30:03.667 --> 00:30:09.707 line:0%
(music)

00:30:09.707 --> 00:30:12.777 line:0%
<i> And a host of others
 on the wing.</i>

00:30:15.847 --> 00:30:18.282 line:0%
<i> The natives are welcome back.</i>

00:30:18.282 --> 00:30:22.619 line:0%
<i> But some visitors here
 are outsiders.</i>

00:30:22.619 --> 00:30:24.922 line:0%
<i> The miners who used
 to work this area</i>

00:30:24.922 --> 00:30:29.827 line:0%
<i> left behind more than
 waste and ruins.</i>

00:30:29.827 --> 00:30:31.295 line:0%
<i> They're most likely the ones</i>

00:30:31.295 --> 00:30:34.999 line:0%
<i> who introduced
 a most destructive new species.</i>

00:30:44.174 --> 00:30:47.345 line:0%
<i> These are feral burros.</i>

00:30:50.081 --> 00:30:55.686 line:0%
<i> These wild donkeys travel
 up to 40 miles a day</i>

00:30:55.686 --> 00:31:00.057 line:0%
<i> throughout California's
 Death Valley area</i>

00:31:00.057 --> 00:31:02.760 line:0%
<i> in search of anything green.</i>

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:04.795 line:0%
(music)

00:31:04.795 --> 00:31:10.701 line:0%
(music)

00:31:10.701 --> 00:31:15.372 line:0%
<i> They use roads, the paths
 of least resistance,</i>

00:31:15.372 --> 00:31:17.875 line:0%
<i> to skip the rockiest terrain</i>

00:31:17.875 --> 00:31:21.045 line:0%
<i> and often head towards
 Mount Whitney.</i>

00:31:22.946 --> 00:31:24.482 line:0%
<i> They're wasteful eaters</i>

00:31:24.482 --> 00:31:28.453 line:0%
<i> and quickly destroy plants
 that take years to grow.</i>

00:31:31.021 --> 00:31:36.494 line:0%
<i> Worse still, the burros
 are prolific breeders.</i>

00:31:36.494 --> 00:31:40.598 line:0%
<i> Herds can double in size
 in four or five years.</i>

00:31:42.800 --> 00:31:47.972 line:0%
<i> Half a million burros
 now roam the countryside.</i>

00:31:47.972 --> 00:31:50.241 line:0%
<i> Their invasion is bad news</i>

00:31:50.241 --> 00:31:53.944 line:0%
<i> for some residents
 of the Death Valley area.</i>

00:31:53.944 --> 00:31:58.316 line:0%
(music)

00:31:58.316 --> 00:32:01.252 line:0%
<i> The largest native animal
 in these parts...</i>

00:32:04.755 --> 00:32:07.391 line:0%
<i> the desert bighorn sheep.</i>

00:32:07.391 --> 00:32:09.426 line:0%
(music)

00:32:09.426 --> 00:32:14.765 line:0%
(music)

00:32:14.765 --> 00:32:18.035 line:0%
<i> These sure-footed nomads
 comb the hillsides</i>

00:32:18.035 --> 00:32:22.706 line:0%
<i> for the most nutritious plants,
 shrubs and even cactus.</i>

00:32:22.706 --> 00:32:25.509 line:0%
(music)

00:32:25.509 --> 00:32:30.647 line:0%
(music)

00:32:30.647 --> 00:32:34.151 line:0%
<i> But their main goal
 is to find water.</i>

00:32:34.151 --> 00:32:37.821 line:0%
(music)

00:32:37.821 --> 00:32:41.959 line:0%
<i> They need to find a spring or
 a water hole every three days</i>

00:32:41.959 --> 00:32:45.395 line:0%
<i> to survive the summer heat.</i>

00:32:45.395 --> 00:32:48.298 line:0%
<i> But with that,
 they can climb ever higher</i>

00:32:48.298 --> 00:32:51.202 line:0%
<i> towards the cool mountain air.</i>

00:32:57.742 --> 00:33:01.579 line:0%
<i> The ultramarathon runners
 have the same idea.</i>

00:33:01.579 --> 00:33:06.651 line:0%
(music)

00:33:06.651 --> 00:33:08.519 line:0%
<i> They start at below sea level</i>

00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:11.722 line:0%
<i> at the lowest point
 in the United States.</i>

00:33:11.722 --> 00:33:17.828 line:0%
(music)

00:33:17.828 --> 00:33:23.735 line:0%
<i> Now they are at 4,000 feet
 altitude and still climbing.</i>

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:28.272 line:0%
<i> The mountains ahead
 mark their finish line</i>

00:33:28.272 --> 00:33:31.174 line:0%
<i> at the base of Mount Whitney,</i>

00:33:31.174 --> 00:33:34.645 line:0%
<i> the highest peak
 in the Lower 48 states.</i>

00:33:34.645 --> 00:33:40.317 line:0%
(music)

00:33:40.317 --> 00:33:42.920 line:0%
<i> Along the road to Whitney,</i>

00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:46.824 line:0%
<i> a host of all-terrain animals
 that can handle the desert</i>

00:33:46.824 --> 00:33:49.394 line:0%
<i> and the heights.</i>

00:33:52.496 --> 00:33:57.601 line:0%
<i> Coyotes are tough enough
 to hunt up here.</i>

00:33:57.601 --> 00:34:01.505 line:0%
<i> This is likely a breeding pair,</i>

00:34:01.505 --> 00:34:04.942 line:0%
<i> and they work together
 to track down prey.</i>

00:34:04.942 --> 00:34:07.778 line:0%
(music)

00:34:07.778 --> 00:34:14.685 line:0%
(music)

00:34:14.685 --> 00:34:18.689 line:0%
<i> Not such good news for
 their favorite menu item.</i>

00:34:21.625 --> 00:34:24.662 line:0%
<i> Desert hares are also climbers.</i>

00:34:27.497 --> 00:34:29.600 line:0%
<i> Some black-tailed jackrabbits
 hang out</i>

00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:33.304 line:0%
<i> at elevations
 up to 12,000 feet.</i>

00:34:33.304 --> 00:34:40.310 line:0%
(music)

00:34:40.310 --> 00:34:44.014 line:0%
<i> But they are best known
 as desert dwellers.</i>

00:34:44.014 --> 00:34:48.052 line:0%
(music)

00:34:48.052 --> 00:34:53.791 line:0%
(music)

00:34:53.791 --> 00:34:56.661 line:0%
<i> And they have a body to suit.</i>

00:34:58.396 --> 00:35:01.632 line:0%
<i> Those ears act like
 an air conditioner.</i>

00:35:01.632 --> 00:35:05.336 line:0%
<i> It's where they release
 their excess body heat.</i>

00:35:08.306 --> 00:35:11.709 line:0%
<i> Those bunny ears are so good
 at what they do,</i>

00:35:11.709 --> 00:35:17.848 line:0%
<i> these hares don't need to pant
 or sweat, and that saves water.</i>

00:35:17.848 --> 00:35:23.954 line:0%
(music)

00:35:23.954 --> 00:35:28.759 line:0%
<i> The only thing more important
 to this guy than his big ears</i>

00:35:28.759 --> 00:35:30.894 line:0%
<i> are his big feet.</i>

00:35:30.894 --> 00:35:34.932 line:0%
(music)

00:35:34.932 --> 00:35:40.938 line:0%
(music)

00:35:40.938 --> 00:35:43.007 line:0%
<i> With those coyotes
 getting closer,</i>

00:35:43.007 --> 00:35:46.077 line:0%
<i> they're his best chance
 for escape.</i>

00:35:48.512 --> 00:35:50.748 line:0%
<i> The chase is on.</i>

00:35:50.748 --> 00:35:51.983 line:0%
(howling)

00:35:55.819 --> 00:36:00.958 line:0%
<i> Black-tailed jackrabbits
 are speed demons.</i>

00:36:00.958 --> 00:36:03.227 line:0%
<i> Not much moves faster
 through the desert</i>

00:36:03.227 --> 00:36:06.864 line:0%
<i> below California's
 Mount Whitney.</i>

00:36:06.864 --> 00:36:10.200 line:0%
<i> Especially when that black tail
 is being chased</i>

00:36:10.200 --> 00:36:12.669 line:0%
<i> by a couple of coyotes.</i>

00:36:12.669 --> 00:36:19.609 line:0%
(music)

00:36:19.609 --> 00:36:23.347 line:0%
<i> These rabbits can reach
 40 miles an hour</i>

00:36:23.347 --> 00:36:28.118 line:0%
<i> and zig-zag through any terrain
 to throw off a rival.</i>

00:36:28.118 --> 00:36:33.057 line:0%
<i> If he has to, he can cover
 20 feet in a single leap.</i>

00:36:36.727 --> 00:36:39.864 line:0%
(howl)

00:36:39.864 --> 00:36:44.101 line:0%
<i> Today, it's enough
 to throw off the coyotes.</i>

00:36:46.604 --> 00:36:49.574 line:0%
<i> For them, it's back
 to the grind.</i>

00:36:55.479 --> 00:36:57.748 line:0%
<i> Not all coyotes
 are lucky enough</i>

00:36:57.748 --> 00:37:00.617 line:0%
<i> to score a luxury resort.</i>

00:37:00.617 --> 00:37:02.886 line:0%
(music)

00:37:02.886 --> 00:37:09.793 line:0%
(music)

00:37:09.793 --> 00:37:14.732 line:0%
<i> More often out here,
 it's like this...</i>

00:37:14.732 --> 00:37:17.133 line:0%
<i> hot as hell,</i>

00:37:17.133 --> 00:37:20.137 line:0%
<i> chasing elusive jackrabbits.</i>

00:37:21.672 --> 00:37:25.910 line:0%
<i> You have to get water
 when you can,</i>

00:37:25.910 --> 00:37:28.346 line:0%
<i> wherever you can.</i>

00:37:30.213 --> 00:37:33.517 line:0%
<i> A leaky pipe couldn't
 be better.</i>

00:37:33.517 --> 00:37:35.285 line:0%
(music)

00:37:35.285 --> 00:37:41.325 line:0%
(music)

00:37:41.325 --> 00:37:47.665 line:0%
(music)

00:37:47.665 --> 00:37:50.534 line:0%
<i> It's also a single-drop shower.</i>

00:37:50.534 --> 00:37:57.508 line:0%
(music)

00:37:57.508 --> 00:38:04.548 line:0%
(music)

00:38:04.548 --> 00:38:07.584 line:0%
<i> And when the rabbits
 are too darn fast,</i>

00:38:07.584 --> 00:38:11.756 line:0%
<i> there's always the spoils
 from Highway 34.</i>

00:38:13.790 --> 00:38:18.996 line:0%
<i> Tourists drop all manner
 of food just for the coyotes.</i>

00:38:18.996 --> 00:38:23.901 line:0%
<i> It's a quick feed that
 does more harm than good.</i>

00:38:25.902 --> 00:38:29.006 line:0%
<i> She's lured close to the road.</i>

00:38:31.342 --> 00:38:37.114 line:0%
<i> The most dangerous place for a
 coyote in all of Death Valley.</i>

00:38:39.950 --> 00:38:44.287 line:0%
<i> If a coyote, or any animal,
 gets hit by a car,</i>

00:38:44.287 --> 00:38:49.293 line:0%
<i> they can expect to be mopped up
 by an unsavory clean-up crew.</i>

00:38:52.496 --> 00:38:56.099 line:0%
<i> Turkey vultures.</i>

00:38:56.099 --> 00:38:57.667 line:0%
<i> Already they seem to wonder</i>

00:38:57.667 --> 00:39:01.405 line:0%
<i> what roadkill coyote
 might taste like.</i>

00:39:05.475 --> 00:39:08.945 line:0%
<i> Most of them wait above
 the road to Mount Whitney</i>

00:39:08.945 --> 00:39:11.849 line:0%
<i> with little interest
 in the living.</i>

00:39:15.585 --> 00:39:20.524 line:0%
<i> They've chosen one of the only
 trees around for a roost.</i>

00:39:22.426 --> 00:39:26.229 line:0%
<i> The desert conditions
 are unbearable for most,</i>

00:39:26.229 --> 00:39:30.767 line:0%
<i> but these vultures have
 a trick up their sleeves,</i>

00:39:30.767 --> 00:39:33.971 line:0%
<i> or rather, down their legs.</i>

00:39:35.572 --> 00:39:39.744 line:0%
<i> They pee on themselves
 to keep from overheating.</i>

00:39:41.912 --> 00:39:47.017 line:0%
<i> A process called urohidrosis.</i>

00:39:47.017 --> 00:39:49.520 line:0%
<i> The urine is also
 a disinfectant</i>

00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:52.456 line:0%
<i> that kills germs on their feet.</i>

00:39:52.456 --> 00:39:57.061 line:0%
<i> Handy when you tuck your talons
 into dead things for a living.</i>

00:39:58.963 --> 00:40:01.198 line:0%
<i> Time for work.</i>

00:40:04.134 --> 00:40:08.305 line:0%
<i> Meet the vulture club.</i>

00:40:08.305 --> 00:40:10.608 line:0%
<i> Members climb on
 thermals of hot air</i>

00:40:10.608 --> 00:40:14.245 line:0%
<i> that rise around
 California's Mount Whitney.</i>

00:40:17.981 --> 00:40:23.187 line:0%
<i> The turkey vulture's six-foot
 wingspan makes it look easy.</i>

00:40:26.590 --> 00:40:32.930 line:0%
<i> They can soar as far as 200
 miles, if the wind is right.</i>

00:40:35.999 --> 00:40:41.338 line:0%
<i> Each turkey vulture relies on
 its powerful sense of smell.</i>

00:40:41.338 --> 00:40:43.373 line:0%
(music)

00:40:43.373 --> 00:40:49.546 line:0%
(music)

00:40:49.546 --> 00:40:52.015 line:0%
<i> One homes in on a new scent.</i>

00:40:52.015 --> 00:40:54.051 line:0%
(music)

00:40:54.051 --> 00:41:00.123 line:0%
(music)

00:41:00.123 --> 00:41:04.361 line:0%
<i> A jackrabbit met
 an untimely end.</i>

00:41:04.361 --> 00:41:08.832 line:0%
(music)

00:41:08.832 --> 00:41:12.536 line:0%
<i> The vulture does its best
 to eat quickly.</i>

00:41:14.604 --> 00:41:18.409 line:0%
<i> Other dinner guests
 are never far behind.</i>

00:41:21.878 --> 00:41:27.050 line:0%
<i> Their stomach acid is at least
 10 times stronger than our own.</i>

00:41:27.050 --> 00:41:31.355 line:0%
<i> Their biggest worry
 isn't fast food,</i>

00:41:31.355 --> 00:41:33.623 line:0%
<i> but a fast car.</i>

00:41:33.623 --> 00:41:38.662 line:0%
(music)

00:41:38.662 --> 00:41:45.336 line:0%
(music)

00:41:45.336 --> 00:41:47.370 line:0%
<i> Just up the road,</i>

00:41:47.370 --> 00:41:50.040 line:0%
<i> the snow-marked peaks
 of the High Sierras</i>

00:41:50.040 --> 00:41:54.078 line:0%
<i> are a welcome sight for
 the ultramarathon runners.</i>

00:41:56.313 --> 00:42:01.718 line:0%
<i> They've covered 122 grueling
 miles to get this far.</i>

00:42:01.718 --> 00:42:05.789 line:0%
(music)

00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:07.991 line:0%
<i> Just 13 more to go.</i>

00:42:07.991 --> 00:42:14.798 line:0%
(music)

00:42:14.798 --> 00:42:18.635 line:0%
<i> 13 miles in another world.</i>

00:42:18.635 --> 00:42:22.873 line:0%
(music)

00:42:22.873 --> 00:42:27.511 line:0%
<i> It's steep as they head through
 the town of Lone Pine.</i>

00:42:27.511 --> 00:42:30.347 line:0%
<i> Some are down to a walk,</i>

00:42:30.347 --> 00:42:32.382 line:0%
<i> but that's better than a crawl.</i>

00:42:32.382 --> 00:42:36.386 line:0%
(music)

00:42:36.386 --> 00:42:41.591 line:0%
<i> With aching joints
 and pounding feet,</i>

00:42:41.591 --> 00:42:43.594 line:0%
<i> they cross the finish line.</i>

00:42:43.594 --> 00:42:49.900 line:0%
(cheering)

00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:55.973 line:0%
<i> They celebrate the end
 of a grueling journey</i>

00:42:55.973 --> 00:43:00.811 line:0%
<i> from the lowest and hottest
 place in America,</i>

00:43:00.811 --> 00:43:06.984 line:0%
<i> to the highest and one of the
 coldest peaks in the Lower 48.</i>

00:43:06.984 --> 00:43:10.988 line:0%
<i> The runners learn what the
 animals here have long known.</i>

00:43:10.988 --> 00:43:14.925 line:0%
<i> Life in this corridor
 is less about a race,</i>

00:43:14.925 --> 00:43:17.727 line:0%
<i> and more about survival.</i>

00:43:17.727 --> 00:43:23.666 line:0%
<i> Even the luxury golf course has
 more traps than meet the eye.</i>

00:43:23.666 --> 00:43:27.938 line:0%
<i> Most creatures have
 to fight for life.</i>

00:43:27.938 --> 00:43:31.675 line:0%
<i> Every day is a scramble,</i>

00:43:31.675 --> 00:43:36.079 line:0%
<i> where animals have
 to watch each step</i>

00:43:36.079 --> 00:43:39.783 line:0%
<i> and beat the heat
 as best they can.</i>

00:43:41.051 --> 00:43:45.455 line:0%
<i> The 146-mile path
 to Mount Whitney</i>

00:43:45.455 --> 00:43:47.858 line:0%
<i> offers some relief.</i>

00:43:49.660 --> 00:43:53.597 line:0%
<i> But more extremes await
 at the other end.</i>

00:43:53.597 --> 00:43:58.468 line:0%
<i> And a wrong turn
 can be your last.</i>

00:43:58.468 --> 00:44:01.138 line:0%
<i> But survive this world,</i>

00:44:01.138 --> 00:44:05.008 line:0%
<i> and you know you've done
 something incredible;</i>

00:44:05.008 --> 00:44:09.647 line:0%
<i> you've conquered the path
 of two great extremes.</i>

